      "valueCode": "unknown"
    } ]
  } ],
  "purpose": "(Clinical Focus: These codes represent the specific function performed or authorized for a participant in a healthcare service or act (e.g., primary care physician, care team roles, sponsor/underwriter roles, consent-related roles).),(Data Element Scope: Used to encode participant function within clinical, administrative, or consent workflows—i.e., how an actor participates in an act—drawing codes from the HL7 v3 ParticipationFunction code system (http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ParticipationFunction). Implementations typically bind this set to elements that qualify a participant’s role/function in an encounter, order, documentation, coverage, or consent context.),(Inclusion Criteria: Includes all codes defined in HL7 v3 ParticipationFunction, including its named subsets (e.g., AuthorizedParticipationFunction, ConsenterParticipationFunction, Sponsor/UnderwriterParticipationFunction, and provider functions such as PCP)),(Exclusion Criteria: Does not include codes from other HL7 v3 participation vocabularies (e.g., ParticipationType) and any local or site-specific extensions not present in the HL7 v3 ParticipationFunction code system)",
